reg canon: shell/systemd tooling — rsync(1) flags (--delete, --dry-run, -a), systemctl --user units (.service/.timer, OnCalendar), systemd.unit(5) specifiers, cp -a/tar-pipe fallback, realpath(1), diff -r/xattr-free comparison.
inv: SRC := /opt/data/workspace/hermes-context/, DST := /workspace/hermes-context/ (override via HERMES_CONTEXT_SRC/DST).
inv: CONTENTS sync: SRC/ -> DST, ∀ never SRC -> DST/SRC (no nesting).
inv: A2_one_way: ∀ run -> writes only to DST, host mount read-only.
inv: A5_mirror: ∀ path ∈ {rsync, cp-fallback} -> DST end state == SRC end state (exact mirror; rsync via --delete, fallback via full reconcile), recursive.
inv: A6_dryrun_purity: --dry-run -> ∀ bytes written = 0, logs included, DST byte-identical post-run.
inv: A7: mirror is recursive; fallback deletes stale subtrees ∀ depth.
inv: A8: LOG path ∉ DST ∀ mode; install paths (∼/.local/bin) ∉ DST; sync never deletes own entrypoints.
inv: A9_mirror_class: mirror ≡ {file contents, dir structure (recursive), symlinks}; metadata/timestamps/hardlinks ∉ class; verify fails nonzero on mismatch, never warn-and-exit-0.
inv: A10_bar: FAIL ⇔ defect reachable in normal operation (default config, documented usage, plausible misconfig losing data); exotic triggers -> KNOWN_LIMITATIONS (+open), non-blocking.
inv: A11: guard SRC==DST (reject/clean no-op); ∀ rm -rf DST ⇒ ∃ verified copy of SRC elsewhere; source survival > freshness.
inv: A12_path_identity: guard via realpath(SRC)/realpath(DST) — reject (nonzero, no writes) iff equal | ancestor/descendant | DST resolves into SRC; applies ∀ sync path, pre-destructive.
inv: A13_order: stage -> verify (content-compare, A9 class) -> then touch DST; unverified copy ≠ "verified" in README.
inv: A3_standalone: script runs sans systemd; units are USER units (systemctl --user), no root.
inv: timer cadence: 6h (OnCalendar), idempotent run, one-line summary log per real run.
resolved: A1..A13 folded; no remaining questions.
open: KNOWN_LIMITATIONS candidates (per A10): newline-in-filename corpora edge cases in fallback diff; DST resolved-through-symlink-to-log-dir hostile env combos — repro notes only.
